    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d297">

                <pb facs="0369" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 PW/2–1347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to General of the Army Douglas
                        MacArthur, at Tokyo</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-02-13T18:00:00-05:00">February 13,
                            1947—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Personal for General MacArthur from Ambassador Atcheson. Understand that
                    advanced transfer paper introduced today in FEC against background of US Govt
                    decision to issue interim directive if Commission does not act favorably on
                    paper in question within approximately 2 weeks.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d297-f1"/>
                    [Atcheson.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d297-f1" n="35" xml:id="d297-f1-content">
                <p>For report on action taken, see telegram 54 (FEC 8), February 19, to Tokyo, <ref
                        target="#pg359">p. 359</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
